WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.175 --> 00:00:03.245
[music]

2
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.510
[Instructor] So we've gotten to move
around our

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.910
Animator window just a little bit.

4
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.560
And we've gotten to go,
and look into

5
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.447
some of the animations themselves,

6
00:00:15.658 --> 00:00:17.668
and preview them.

7
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.440
And we've seen some of the movement

8
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.450
between all of the transitions.

9
00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.906
So now what we're going to do is
we're actually going to play around

10
00:00:26.906 --> 00:00:29.242
with the values
in these transitions.

11
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:33.030
So knowing that our transition
for our "Speed"

12
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:35.648
needs to greater than .25

13
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.275
to be able to start
this "Walk_Static" animation,

14
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.700
we can actually go
over on the left side

15
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.944
of the Animator window
to Parameters.

16
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.556
And if we click this tab,

17
00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:50.333
we have a Parameter section that opens.

18
00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:54.314
And here you can actually see
the Parameter of the Speed...

19
00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:57.543
that we can set. So in fact,

20
00:00:57.543 --> 00:01:00.263
if we make this for example .3

21
00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.962
because .3 is greater than .25,

22
00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:08.422
and now when we press Play in our game,
we can actually see

23
00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.980
when the Player enters the game,

24
00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:13.150
then it should go into the "Idle" state,

25
00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:16.159
and then it'll go down
to the Walk_Static state.

26
00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.020
So we're an in Idle,
and then it starts Walking.

27
00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.973
Now, it looks a little weird,
because the Background

28
00:01:26.973 --> 00:01:30.724
is moving incredibly fast compared
to the actual Player.

29
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.162
So let's see what kinda speed
that we need to have.

30
00:01:34.162 --> 00:01:36.710
We need greater than .5,
so we'll make this...

31
00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:39.020
we'll just make this 1.

32
00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:42.215
So that's definitely,
definitely more than .5.

33
00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.360
So we press Play.

34
00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.560
There you go. And then you can
see it goes from the Walking

35
00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.080
to the running animation.
Now that does look kinda weird

36
00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.080
because the scene is just moving,
so we can actually

37
00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.370
set a default animation state.

38
00:01:57.370 --> 00:01:59.377
So if we go to our "Run_Static" here,

39
00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:02.230
and we right click on it,

40
00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:05.190
we can actually
"Set as Layer Default State."

41
00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:09.055
So if we select that,
you can see our entry state

42
00:02:09.055 --> 00:02:11.067
goes directly to our Run_Static

43
00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:15.170
instead of to Idle because from Idle,
we had to go to Walk_Static

44
00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:17.520
all the way to Run_Static,
and that just took way too long.

45
00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.280
So now when we press Play,

46
00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:24.430
you can see that the Player
starts running.

47
00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.562
The animation's still
a little too slow,

48
00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.760
but we can fix that really easily.

49
00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:33.250
So you can see on our
different states

50
00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:35.718
there's actually some information
in the Inspector.

51
00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:41.754
So you can see actually, the Speed
of which the animation runs.

52
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.820
So since the Player looked like 
they were running a little slow,

53
00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.636
comparatively we'll set
this to something like 1.5.

54
00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:51.833
And now we'll Play this animation.

55
00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.480
And there you go, now it looks
like the Player's really running,

56
00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.978
and then they jump, and they're still
running. But that's fine,

57
00:02:59.263 --> 00:03:01.110
we can fix that at some point.

58
00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.110
Now they're just moving so fast

59
00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.590
that they just end up back
in the same place on earth.

60
00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.890
And then one more thing
that you can see

61
00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:11.890
is you can actually see different

62
00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.044
animation Layers which we'll go into.

63
00:03:15.044 --> 00:03:18.020
But it's just kind of interesting
to see how they all work.

64
00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:20.030
So with the Idle, you know,

65
00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:23.259
you can see all of these different
Idle states that it can go into.

66
00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:26.530
With jumping, you can go from Idle
to a "Standing_Jump"

67
00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.530
or "Walk," and then "Walking_Jump."

68
00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:33.168
There's different ways
of dying, or crouching.

69
00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:36.653
So there's all of these different kinds
of animation states that we can control,

70
00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.043
based on certain conditions.

71
00:03:39.433 --> 00:03:41.560
So what you're going to do

72
00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:44.720
is you're going to start using
some animations of your own.

73
00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:48.113
So make sure that you click
on the Player in the Hierarchy.

74
00:03:48.797 --> 00:03:50.828
In their Animator Component,

75
00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.290
you're going to double-click
on the Controller

76
00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.346
which will then open up
your Animator window.

77
00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.210
In your Animator window,
you're going to move

78
00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.520
with either alt and left clicking,

79
00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:06.291
or pressing down your mouse wheel,
and dragging around.

80
00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:11.424
You're going to find Run_Static,
right click on it,

81
00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.878
set it as the default Layer state.

82
00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.524
And then in your Parameters,

83
00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:23.778
you're going to set
your "Speed_f" to 1.

84
00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.089
And then inside

85
00:04:27.089 --> 00:04:29.250
of your Inspector

86
00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:32.982
if you have one of the
animation states highlighted,

87
00:04:32.982 --> 00:04:34.990
specifically Run_Static,

88
00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:38.569
you can change the speed
that the animation runs itself.

89
00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.880
And so we're going to make
it a little faster

90
00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.334
than the standard animation speed.

91
00:04:43.914 --> 00:04:47.771
We'll make it about 1.5,
and then you can press Play.

92
00:04:48.996 --> 00:04:51.769
And then we can really see
our Player running through the scene.

93
00:04:52.607 --> 00:04:55.678
And they're so happy
because they're in the wilderness.

94
00:04:56.985 --> 00:04:58.915
Now it's your turn.

95
00:04:59.242 --> 00:05:01.452
[music]
